      "status": "ready",
      "data": {
        "bridge": "这是整体使用的条件连接表达，把“可以继续”与“负责人确认范围”连接起来。后半句给出成立条件。",
        "bridgeHistory": "provided作为条件连接词已有长期记录。本句直接使用这一条件分支，that引出条件内容。",
        "bridgeTarget": "sense-0"
      },
      "provenance": {
        "historyRelation": "editorial_link_to_sourced_history",
        "sourceRefs": [
          {
            "sourceId": "cambridge-provided",
            "sourceVersion": "2026-11-16",
            "locator": "conjunction, also provided that",
            "supportedClaim": "provided that引出条件；不能删除其条件从句。",
            "url": "https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/provided"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "V20261012-100",
      "contextId": "V20261012-100-context",
      "inputHash": "a813bbfc55f7d1e5e1411123b927662ccb99f136f39bfe589bd56616e6bfc398",
      "status": "ready",
      "data": {
        "bridge": "它否定的是“任务完成就一定代表问题解决”这层必然联系。完成与解决可能同时发生，但前者不能保证后者。",
        "bridgeHistory": "necessarily的必然结果义有历史记录；加上not后，当前表达取消必然性。这是现代组合解释，组成词的年代不代表整个短语的起源年代。",
        "bridgeTarget": "sense-0"
      },
      "provenance": {
        "historyRelation": "editorial_link_to_sourced_history",
        "sourceRefs": [
          {
            "sourceId": "cambridge-necessarily",
            "sourceVersion": "2026-11-16",
            "locator": "not necessarily",
            "supportedClaim": "not necessarily是否定必然性，不是断言相反命题。",
            "url": "https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/learner-english/necessarily"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
